+## opencode-zen / opencode-go — free-tier daily-quota retry-after-ms
+On the free / metered tier of both `opencode-zen` (`https://opencode.ai/zen`) and `opencode-go` (`https://opencode.ai/zen/go`), daily-quota reset responses return `HTTP 429` with `retry-after-ms=21431000` (≈5h 57m). The shared retry layer (`fetchWithRetry.maxDelayMs` = 60s and `retry.maxDelayMs` = 5 min in `packages/ai/src/utils/fetch-with-retry.ts` and `packages/ai/src/utils/retry.ts`) caps each sleep at the configured ceiling, so the hint exceeds both caps and surfaces as a hard error rather than a quiet wait-until-quota-resets retry.
+
+Fix: add `retry: { unboundedRetryAfter: true }` to the `ProviderDefinition` (`packages/ai/src/registry/opencode-zen.ts`, `packages/ai/src/registry/opencode-go.ts`) — one line per provider file — which lifts both caps for `Retry-After`/`retry-after-ms` hints. The user setting `providers.unboundedRetryAfter` (string array, default `["opencode-go", "opencode-zen"]`) can also flip the behavior at runtime without touching provider files. See [docs/non-compaction-retry-policy.md#per-provider-unbounded-retry-after](./non-compaction-retry-policy.md#per-provider-unbounded-retry-after) for the full plumbing.
